window.__finlexDocLoaded(10220,{"id":10220,"articles":[{"id":1000929,"no":"Overview","heading":"Scope & Core Objective (Public Summary)","text":"Applies the acquisition method to business combinations (measuring identifiable assets, liabilities, and noncontrolling interests at fair value), including the 'screen test' for asset acquisitions, pushdown accounting option (ASC 805-50), and joint venture formation at fair value (ASU 2023-05).","seq":0},{"id":1000930,"no":"ASC 805-10-55","heading":"Definition of a Business & Mandatory Screen Test","text":"Before applying acquisition accounting, determine whether the acquired set is a BUSINESS or an ASSET ACQUISITION (ASC 805-10-55-3A~9):\n• Mandatory Screen Test (55-5A): If substantially all fair value of the gross assets acquired is concentrated in a single identifiable asset or group of similar identifiable assets, the set is NOT a business (account as an asset acquisition — capitalize transaction costs, no goodwill, no Day-1 bargain purchase gain).\n• Framework when Screen Fails: Must include at minimum an input AND a substantive process that together significantly contribute to the ability to create outputs (higher bar when no outputs exist yet — requires an organized workforce).","seq":1},{"id":1000931,"no":"ASC 805-20 / 30","heading":"Acquisition Method, Full Goodwill, Contingent Consideration & Measurement Period","text":"• Four Steps (ASC 805-10-05-4): (1) Identify acquirer; (2) Determine acquisition date; (3) Recognize & measure identifiable assets acquired, liabilities assumed, and Noncontrolling Interest (NCI); (4) Recognize goodwill or bargain purchase gain.\n• Mandatory Full Goodwill (ASC 805-20-30-1): NCI MUST be measured at acquisition-date FAIR VALUE (incorporating both controlling and NCI goodwill — no partial goodwill option).\n• Acquisition-Related Costs (ASC 805-10-25-23): Expensed as incurred (banker, legal, audit fees).\n• Contingent Consideration / Earn-Outs (ASC 805-30-25-5): Recognized at acquisition-date fair value; liability-classified earn-outs are remeasured to fair value through P&L each period (equity-classified earn-outs are not remeasured).\n• Measurement Period (ASC 805-10-25-13~19): Up to 1 year from acquisition date to finalize provisional fair values; adjustments are recognized in the REPORTING PERIOD identified (ASU 2015-16 — no retrospective restatement of prior comparative periods).","seq":2},{"id":1000932,"no":"ASC 805-50","heading":"Pushdown Accounting, Common-Control Transfers & JV Formations","text":"• Pushdown Accounting Election (ASC 805-50-25-4): An acquired entity may ELECT to apply pushdown accounting in its separate financial statements upon a change-in-control event (stepping up assets/liabilities and recording goodwill on the subsidiary's own books).\n• Common-Control Transactions (ASC 805-50-30-5): Accounted for at historical carrying amounts (carryover basis) with retrospective combination for periods under common control.\n• Joint Venture Formations (ASU 2023-05, ASC 805-60, effective Jan 1, 2025): Newly formed JVs measure contributed net assets at FAIR VALUE upon formation (recognizing goodwill if total JV fair value exceeds identifiable net assets).","seq":3},{"id":1000933,"no":"ASC 805 vs IFRS 3 / CAS 20","heading":"Key Cross-Framework Divergences (US GAAP vs. IFRS 3 vs. CAS 20)","text":"• NCI & Goodwill: ASC 805 mandates Fair Value (full goodwill); IFRS 3 allows transaction-by-transaction choice between fair value and proportionate share of identifiable net assets.\n• Screen Test: Mandatory under ASC 805; optional Concentration Test under IFRS 3.B7B.\n• Pushdown Accounting: Permitted under ASC 805-50; NOT permitted under IFRS.\n• Pre-Acquisition Contingencies: ASC 805-20-25-19 recognizes contingent liabilities at fair value only if determinable during the measurement period (otherwise falls back to ASC 450 probable/estimable); IFRS 3 recognizes all present-obligation contingent liabilities if fair value is reliably measurable.\n• Measurement Period Adjustments: Recognized in current period under ASC 805; applied retrospectively to acquisition date under IFRS 3.45.","seq":4},{"id":1000934,"no":"Official Access","heading":"Official FASB Codification & Reference Entry","text":"Official Portal (FASB Accounting Standards Codification®): https://asc.fasb.org/\nStatus: in_force (FASB ASC free Basic View available at https://asc.fasb.org/).","seq":5}]});
